    "body": "## Change Summary\n\n- `_detect_shard_pattern` in `tools/mcore_checkpoint_convert/utils/ckpt_util.py` recognized shard files with any number of digits but always returned a `{:05d}-of-{:05d}` format string. As a result, `load_huggingface_checkpoint` / `merge_transformers_sharded_states` built the wrong file names for shards that are not padded to exactly 5 digits (for example `model-00001-of-000163.safetensors`) and raised `FileNotFoundError`.\n- The fix uses one regex to match both supported prefixes and builds the format string from the zero-padding widths in the matched filename. Behavior for the existing 5-digit layouts does not change.\n- Fixes #325\n- Affected module: `tools/mcore_checkpoint_convert` (used by the adapter / vision_patch / adapter_internvl / merge_huggingface conversion scripts).\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] I ran the relevant local checks.\n- [x] I added or updated tests where appropriate.\n- [x] I checked compatibility with existing APIs and configurations.\n\nAdded `tests/llm_vlm/unit/test_ckpt_util_shard_pattern.py`, which covers the `model-XXXXX-of-XXXXX`, `model-XXXXX-of-XXXXXX` and `model.safetensors-XXXXX-of-XXXXX` layouts. Before the fix, the 6-digit case fails with `FileNotFoundError`. After the fix, all three cases pass, and so does `tests/llm_vlm/unit/test_convert_checkpoint_config_utils.py`. Ruff (CI rule set) passes on the changed files.\n\n## CI, GPU, and Image Impact\n\n- [ ] This change affects dependencies, Dockerfiles, patches, or runtime environments.\n- [ ] GPU validation is required. Suggested suite: `llm_vlm` / `embodied`.\n- [ ] A local candidate image should be built during GPU validation.\n- [x] No GPU or image validation is required.\n\n## Reviewer Notes\n\nThis only changes how shard file names are reconstructed. It does not change which files are counted or the order they are loaded in.\n",
